IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb5-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), PART XXI -- GENERAL: CONTINUANCE OF BODIES
-- INCORPORATED BY OR UNDER OTHER ACTS OF PARLIAMENT (s 268). Layer 1: the law, objectively. Nothing here takes
-- anyone's point of view.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. The text this was encoded from is a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice
-- Canada consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (last amended 2026-03-26); it is not an official version,
-- and nothing here has been verified against the official text. Contains information licensed under
-- the Open Government Licence - Canada.
--
-- HOW THIS MODULE READS THE TEXT.
--   * The body corporate is described by facts about how it was incorporated: by or under a special Act of
--     Parliament, by or under some other Act of Parliament, or otherwise. The three are plain BOOLEAN inputs,
--     not an enumeration, because the text treats a body corporate as both (a financial institution is
--     "deemed" to fall under another category, subsection (4.2)).
--   * The vote on the special resolution, the right to dissent (s 190) and the class-rights provisions
--     (s 176, s 187) belong to other pieces; each use is a plain input marked "out of range".

§ `Section 268 -- bodies incorporated by or continued under other Acts of Parliament`

§§ `s 268(1) and s 268(4.2) -- the words "charter" and "financial institution"`

-- "Includes" is not "means": the ordinary meaning is an input beside the two listed things.
-- src:3339 | 268 (1) In this section, charter includes
-- src:3340 | (a) an act of incorporation and any amendments thereto; and
-- src:3341 | (b) letters patent of incorporation and any letters patent supplementary thereto.
@ref CBCA s 268(1) (src:3339-3341)
GIVEN `it is a charter in the ordinary meaning of the word` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an act of incorporation or an amendment to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is letters patent of incorporation or letters patent supplementary to them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `charter within s 268(1)` IF
        `it is a charter in the ordinary meaning of the word`
    OR  `it is an act of incorporation or an amendment to it`
    OR  `it is letters patent of incorporation or letters patent supplementary to them`

-- (4.2): a body corporate incorporated or continued under an Act of Parliament to which one of four financial
-- Acts applies is deemed to be incorporated or continued under an Act of Parliament other than this Act or a
-- special Act, "for the purposes of this section".
-- src:3359 | (4.2) For the purposes of this section, every body corporate that is incorporated or continued under an Act of Parliament and to which the Bank Act, the Cooperative Credit Associations Act, the Insurance Companies Act or the Trust and Loan Companies Act applies is deemed to be incorporated or continued by or under an Act of Parliament other than this Act or a special Act.
@ref CBCA s 268(4.2) (src:3359)
GIVEN `the body corporate is incorporated or continued under an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Bank Act applies to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Cooperative Credit Associations Act applies to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Insurance Companies Act applies to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Trust and Loan Companies Act applies to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body corporate is deemed to be incorporated or continued by or under an Act of Parliament other than this Act or a special Act within s 268(4.2)` IF
        `the body corporate is incorporated or continued under an Act of Parliament`
    AND (    `the Bank Act applies to it`
         OR  `the Cooperative Credit Associations Act applies to it`
         OR  `the Insurance Companies Act applies to it`
         OR  `the Trust and Loan Companies Act applies to it`)

§§ `s 268(2) and s 268(2.1) -- amending the charter on a continuance`

-- Both (2) and (2.1) are in connection with a continuance under this Act; the shareholders entitled to vote
-- at annual meetings may, by special resolution, authorize the directors to apply under s 187 and, by the
-- same resolution, make any amendment to the charter that a CBCA corporation could make to its articles.
-- (2) applies "despite the charter" of a special Act body; (2.1) applies "subject to any other Act of
-- Parliament or the charter" of any other body. The same special resolution does both things, so the
-- rule asks whether it was passed.
-- src:3343 | (2) In connection with a continuance under this Act, the shareholders of a body corporate incorporated or continued by or under a special Act of Parliament who are entitled to vote at annual meetings of shareholders may, despite the charter of the body corporate,
-- src:3344 | (a) by special resolution, authorize the directors of the body corporate to apply under section 187 for a certificate of continuance; and
-- src:3345 | (b) by the same resolution, make any amendment to the charter of the body corporate that a corporation incorporated under this Act may make to its articles.
@ref CBCA s 268(2) (src:3343-3345)
GIVEN `it is in connection with a continuance under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate is incorporated or continued by or under a special Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shareholders are entitled to vote at annual meetings of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the shareholders may authorize the directors and amend the charter by special resolution despite the charter within s 268(2)` IF
        `it is in connection with a continuance under this Act`
    AND `the body corporate is incorporated or continued by or under a special Act of Parliament`
    AND `the shareholders are entitled to vote at annual meetings of shareholders`

-- src:3347 | (2.1) In connection with a continuance under this Act, the shareholders of a body corporate incorporated or continued by or under an Act of Parliament, other than this Act or a special Act, who are entitled to vote at annual meetings of shareholders may, subject to any other Act of Parliament or the charter of the body corporate,
-- src:3348 | (a) by special resolution, authorize the directors of the body corporate to apply under section 187 for a certificate of continuance; and
-- src:3349 | (b) by the same resolution, make any amendment to the charter of the body corporate that a corporation incorporated under this Act may make to its articles.
@ref CBCA s 268(2.1) (src:3347-3349)
GIVEN `it is in connection with a continuance under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate is incorporated or continued by or under an Act of Parliament other than this Act or a special Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shareholders are entitled to vote at annual meetings of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another Act of Parliament or the charter of the body corporate forbids it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the shareholders may authorize the directors and amend the charter by special resolution subject to any other Act and the charter within s 268(2.1)` IF
        `it is in connection with a continuance under this Act`
    AND `the body corporate is incorporated or continued by or under an Act of Parliament other than this Act or a special Act`
    AND `the shareholders are entitled to vote at annual meetings of shareholders`
    AND (NOT `another Act of Parliament or the charter of the body corporate forbids it`)

-- (3): "despite subsections (2) and (2.1)": no change of the nature referred to in subsection 176(1) that
-- affects a class or series of shares, unless (a) the charter provides otherwise about an amendment of the
-- nature in paragraph 176(1)(a), (b) or (e), or (b) the holders of the class or series approve it in
-- accordance with section 176. Paragraph (a) reaches only those three paragraphs of s 176(1).
-- src:3351 | (3) Despite subsections (2) and (2.1), the shareholders of a body corporate may not, by a special resolution under any of those subsections, make any change of the nature referred to in subsection 176(1) that affects a class or series of shares, unless
-- src:3352 | (a) the charter of the body corporate otherwise provides in respect of an amendment of the nature referred to in paragraph 176(1)(a), (b) or (e); or
-- src:3353 | (b) the holders of the class or series of shares approve the change in accordance with section 176.
@ref CBCA s 268(3) (src:3351-3353)
GIVEN `the change is of the nature referred to in subsection 176(1) and affects a class or series of shares` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 176 (piece cb4)
      `the change is of the nature referred to in paragraph 176(1)(a), (b) or (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charter of the body corporate otherwise provides in respect of an amendment of that nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holders of the class or series of shares approve the change in accordance with section 176` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the shareholders may make the change by special resolution under subsection 268(2) or (2.1) within s 268(3)` IF
        (NOT `the change is of the nature referred to in subsection 176(1) and affects a class or series of shares`)
    OR  (     `the change is of the nature referred to in paragraph 176(1)(a), (b) or (e)`
          AND `the charter of the body corporate otherwise provides in respect of an amendment of that nature`)
    OR  `the holders of the class or series of shares approve the change in accordance with section 176`

§§ `s 268(4) and s 268(4.1) -- the directors apply for continuance`

-- Only if the articles of continuance make no amendment to the charter other than one required to conform to
-- this Act. "Subject to subsection (6)" is given no effect: (6) lets the Governor in Council require an
-- application, and nothing in it limits the directors' power here (fork F-268(4)-1 in NOTES.md).
-- (4) is for a special Act body "despite the charter"; (4.1) is for any other Act's body "subject to any
-- other Act of Parliament or the charter".
-- src:3355 | (4) Subject to subsection (6), the directors of a body corporate incorporated or continued by or under a special Act of Parliament may, despite the charter of the body corporate, apply under section 187 for a certificate of continuance if the articles of continuance do not make any amendment to the charter of the body corporate other than an amendment required to conform to this Act.
@ref CBCA s 268(4) (src:3355)
GIVEN `the body corporate is incorporated or continued by or under a special Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles of continuance make no amendment to the charter other than an amendment required to conform to this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the directors may apply for a certificate of continuance despite the charter within s 268(4)` IF
        `the body corporate is incorporated or continued by or under a special Act of Parliament`
    AND `the articles of continuance make no amendment to the charter other than an amendment required to conform to this Act`

-- src:3357 | (4.1) Subject to subsection (6), the directors of a body corporate incorporated or continued by or under an Act of Parliament, other than this Act or a special Act, may, subject to any other Act of Parliament or the charter of the body corporate, apply under section 187 for a certificate of continuance if the articles of continuance do not make any amendment to the charter of the body corporate other than an amendment required to conform to this Act.
@ref CBCA s 268(4.1) (src:3357)
GIVEN `the body corporate is incorporated or continued by or under an Act of Parliament other than this Act or a special Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles of continuance make no amendment to the charter other than an amendment required to conform to this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another Act of Parliament or the charter of the body corporate forbids it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the directors may apply for a certificate of continuance subject to any other Act and the charter within s 268(4.1)` IF
        `the body corporate is incorporated or continued by or under an Act of Parliament other than this Act or a special Act`
    AND `the articles of continuance make no amendment to the charter other than an amendment required to conform to this Act`
    AND (NOT `another Act of Parliament or the charter of the body corporate forbids it`)

§§ `s 268(5) -- no dissent`

-- "In respect of an amendment made under subsection (2), (2.1), (3), (4) or (4.1)": any of the five. The
-- right to dissent is s 190's; this rule says only whether s 268(5) removes it.
-- src:3361 | (5) A shareholder is not entitled to dissent under section 190 in respect of an amendment made under subsection (2), (2.1), (3), (4) or (4.1).
@ref CBCA s 268(5) (src:3361)
GIVEN `the amendment is made under subsection 268(2), (2.1), (3), (4) or (4.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a shareholder is not entitled to dissent under section 190 within s 268(5)` IF -- out of range: section 190 (piece cb4)
    `the amendment is made under subsection 268(2), (2.1), (3), (4) or (4.1)`

§§ `s 268(6), s 268(9) -- discretionary continuance and dissolution`

-- (6): the Governor in Council may by order require a body corporate incorporated by or under an Act of
-- Parliament to which the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act does not apply to apply for continuance
-- within a prescribed period, except for four kinds. The order is the Governor in Council's; the rule says
-- whether a body corporate may be required.
-- src:3363 | (6) The Governor in Council may, by order, require that a body corporate incorporated by or under an Act of Parliament to which the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act does not apply, apply for a certificate of continuance under section 187 within any period that may be prescribed except for the following:
-- src:3364 | (a) a bank;
-- src:3365 | (a.1) an association to which the Cooperative Credit Associations Act applies;
-- src:3366 | (b) a company or society to which the Insurance Companies Act applies; and
-- src:3367 | (c) a company to which the Trust and Loan Companies Act applies.
@ref CBCA s 268(6) (src:3363-3367)
GIVEN `the body corporate is incorporated by or under an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act applies to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a bank` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an association to which the Cooperative Credit Associations Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a company or society to which the Insurance Companies Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a company to which the Trust and Loan Companies Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Governor in Council may require the body corporate to apply for a certificate of continuance within s 268(6)` IF
        `the body corporate is incorporated by or under an Act of Parliament`
    AND (NOT `the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act applies to it`)
    AND (NOT `it is a bank`)
    AND (NOT `it is an association to which the Cooperative Credit Associations Act applies`)
    AND (NOT `it is a company or society to which the Insurance Companies Act applies`)
    AND (NOT `it is a company to which the Trust and Loan Companies Act applies`)

-- (9): a body corporate referred to in (6) that does not apply within the prescribed period is dissolved on
-- the expiration of that period. The last day of the period is prescribed (not among the sources).
-- src:3374 | (9) A body corporate referred to in subsection (6) that does not make an application to obtain a certificate of continuance within the period prescribed is dissolved on the expiration of that period.
@ref CBCA s 268(9) (src:3374)
GIVEN `the body corporate is one referred to in subsection 268(6) required to apply by order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate has applied to obtain a certificate of continuance within the period prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date it is asked whether the body corporate is dissolved` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period prescribed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body corporate is dissolved on the expiration of the period within s 268(9)` IF
        `the body corporate is one referred to in subsection 268(6) required to apply by order`
    AND (NOT `the body corporate has applied to obtain a certificate of continuance within the period prescribed`)
    AND `the date it is asked whether the body corporate is dissolved` GREATER THAN `the last day of the period prescribed`

§§ `s 268(8), s 268(8.1) -- fees and the special Act`

-- src:3370 | (8) A body corporate that obtains a certificate of continuance under this section is not required to pay any fees otherwise payable under this Act in respect of such continuance.
@ref CBCA s 268(8) (src:3370)
GIVEN `the body corporate obtains a certificate of continuance under section 268` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body corporate is not required to pay the fees otherwise payable for the continuance within s 268(8)` IF
    `the body corporate obtains a certificate of continuance under section 268`

-- src:3372 | (8.1) On the continuance of a body corporate incorporated by a special Act of Parliament as a corporation under this Act, the special Act ceases to apply to the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 268(8.1) (src:3372)
GIVEN `a body corporate incorporated by a special Act of Parliament is continued as a corporation under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the special Act ceases to apply to the corporation within s 268(8.1)` IF
    `a body corporate incorporated by a special Act of Parliament is continued as a corporation under this Act`

§§ `s 268(10), s 268(11) -- who may not, and who may, apply for continuance`

-- (10): a body corporate to which the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act applies, or any similar body
-- corporate incorporated otherwise than by or under an Act of Parliament, may not apply.
-- src:3376 | (10) A body corporate to which the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act applies or any similar body corporate incorporated otherwise than by or under an Act of Parliament may not apply for a certificate of continuance under section 187.
@ref CBCA s 268(10) (src:3376)
GIVEN `the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act applies to the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a similar body corporate incorporated otherwise than by or under an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body corporate may not apply for a certificate of continuance under section 187 within s 268(10)` IF
        `the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act applies to the body corporate`
    OR  `it is a similar body corporate incorporated otherwise than by or under an Act of Parliament`

-- (11): "Exception for railway companies": a body corporate incorporated by or under a Special Act as defined
-- in section 87 of the Canada Transportation Act may apply.
-- src:3378 | (11) A body corporate that is incorporated by or under a Special Act, as defined in section 87 of the Canada Transportation Act, may apply for a certificate of continuance under section 187.
@ref CBCA s 268(11) (src:3378)
GIVEN `the body corporate is incorporated by or under a Special Act as defined in section 87 of the Canada Transportation Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body corporate may apply for a certificate of continuance under section 187 within s 268(11)` IF
    `the body corporate is incorporated by or under a Special Act as defined in section 87 of the Canada Transportation Act`

-- The two subsections together: (11) is headed "Exception for railway companies" and is read as an exception
-- to (10), so the prohibition does not bite where (11) applies.
-- src:3376 | (10) A body corporate to which the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act applies or any similar body corporate incorporated otherwise than by or under an Act of Parliament may not apply for a certificate of continuance under section 187.
-- src:3377 | Exception for railway companies
-- src:3378 | (11) A body corporate that is incorporated by or under a Special Act, as defined in section 87 of the Canada Transportation Act, may apply for a certificate of continuance under section 187.
@ref CBCA s 268(10), s 268(11) (src:3376 src:3377-3378)
GIVEN `the body corporate may not apply under subsection 268(10)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate may apply under subsection 268(11)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body corporate may apply for a certificate of continuance within s 268(10) and s 268(11)` IF
        `the body corporate may apply under subsection 268(11)`
    OR  (NOT `the body corporate may not apply under subsection 268(10)`)
